<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lü Buwei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 291–235 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lü Buwei was a wealthy merchant who became chancellor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a>. He backed the hostage prince Zichu, who became King Zhuangxiang, and in 249 BCE led the army that annexed the Duchy of Eastern Zhou. He dominated the court during the youth of King Zheng, the future First Emperor, and sponsored the compendium Lüshi Chunqiu, but was dismissed in 237 BCE and took poison two years later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lu-buwei.jpg" alt="Lü Buwei" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 取自清代修《安徽旌德吕氏宗谱》 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%91%82%E4%B8%8D%E9%9F%8B.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
